# tests/chat-tools-direct, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): evaluating
# this directory yields the test's ARG TREE, which dev/run-test then runs.
#
# A WORKER TEST of llm-step's INLINE TREE TOOLS `copy`, `move` and `remove`: what
# the worker does with a queued batch of them, including the cases that go wrong
# (existing destination, missing source, move into itself, `.caos`) and the ones
# that cross a source tree boundary (a copy of a whole source tree, a copy into
# one, removing one). Like tests/chat-tools it mints the human turn itself and
# reads the turn commit back, because the subject is the worker, not `chat`.
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/worker-test --worker1:@=worker.sh --bash:@=DEEP-DEPS/bash --llm-step:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-step --stub:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-stub --tool:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-test-tool --common:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-test/worker-common.sh
